+## Shared repository service (Ash protocol patch)
+
+`tgrep shared-serve <root> --index-path <cache> --no-require-git` serves independently registered worktrees from one repository. `tgrep identity <root>` returns the canonical Git common directory, or the root for a plain directory. This explicit service uses JSON-RPC capabilities version 1; ordinary `serve`, CLI discovery and existing index readers retain their existing contracts.
+
+RPC operations are `capabilities`, `attach(root, expected_head?)`, `search(worktree_id, ...)`, `files(worktree_id, ...)`, `refresh(worktree_id, paths?)`, `reload(worktree_id)`, `status(worktree_id)` and `detach(worktree_id)`. Paths in a refresh are relative to the registered worktree. Search accepts `max_results` (1–5001) as a global row limit and returns paths in order. Registrations of the same root are reference counted. Another repository is rejected.
+
+Bases are immutable generations keyed by Git tree, index format and file-size profile. They contain committed blobs without running checkout hooks or filters. Decoded content identities decide reuse against each actual worktree, including checkout transformations, committed branch differences, untracked files and ignore changes. Unborn repositories and plain directories use an empty base and a private content overlay. Bases live outside disposable worktrees; delta checkpoints bind the exact base bytes and root. Startup reconciles restored checkpoints before answering indexed queries.
+
+Each view owns its watcher, membership and visibility. Known edits are acknowledged by `refresh`; notifications and the 120-second reconciliation interval are checked before the next request. Initial attach reads eligible contents to establish trusted identities; later reconciliation rereads changed versions and explicitly notified paths. No shared content cache is keyed only by relative filename. Incomplete traversal or unstable reads return errors. Queries in other established worktrees do not take the base-build lock.
